From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] controller: serialize command result sessions

The controller command listener accepts a new TLS client immediately after it
queues an asynchronous request, but stores the connection in one shared m_ssl
pointer. A second client can therefore overwrite the first request's result
session before the manager thread calls send_result(). More importantly, the
listener resets the same m_cmd object while the manager thread is copying and
serializing the response. That race can strand the client in SSL_read forever;
the WebUI then blocks every live REST route behind its native-command mutex.

Keep one result session outstanding at a time. The listener waits for the
manager thread to send and close the result before accepting another client,
with a ten-second absolute deadline that closes an abandoned session. Protect
m_ssl with a mutex/condition pair and defer m_cmd.reset() until the result has
completed.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 inc/em_cmd_ctrl.h         |  8 ++++-
 src/ctrl/em_cmd_ctrl.cpp | 80 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 2 files changed, 76 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

